# A to-do list: a button inside each item (it uses the item), two buttons with the same words, a press that
# fails part way and changes nothing, and a list that learns what it holds.
# do: press "Add"
# do: type "New task" "Write the docs"
# do: press "Add"
# do: type "New task" "Ship it"
# do: press "Add"
# do: type "New task" "Write the docs"
# do: press "Add"
# do: press "Done" 1
# do: press "Done" 1
# do: press "Add all"

Screen Tasks:
  Remember tasks as a list of text, starting at []
  Remember done starting at 0
  Remember new task as text, starting at ""
  Show a heading: "Tasks ({the count of tasks})"
  Show a text box "New task" for new task
  Show a button "Add" (off when new task is empty):
    When pressed:
      When tasks contains new task:
        Stop with "\"{new task}\" is on the list already."
      Add new task to tasks
      Set new task to ""
  Show a list with each task in tasks:
    Show a row:
      Show task
      Show a button "Done":
        When pressed:
          Remove task from tasks
          Increase done by 1
  Show "Done so far: {done}"
  Show a button "Add all":
    When pressed:
      Increase done by 100
      Add "one" to tasks
      Stop with "Nothing was added: this press stops after changing things."
